"Joker" is "poker" with a "J"!

278
00:11:45,471 --> 00:11:46,701
Coincidence?

279
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:49,900
That's "joincidence" with a "C"!

280
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:55,880
Look!

281
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,920
Ugly Naked Guy lit a bunch of candles.

282
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:06,780
That had to hurt!

283
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:12,140
Hey, it's your Thanksgiving too.

284
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:13,820
Instead of watching football,

285
00:12:13,830 --> 00:12:14,500
you could help.

286
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:15,560
We know.

287
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:19,740
Rachel, you want to put the marshmallows

288
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:20,940
in concentric circles.

289
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:21,740
No, Mon.

290
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,880
You want to put them in concentric circles.

291
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:25,900
I want to do this.

292
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:36,520
Every year.

293
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:41,820
It's stuck!

294
00:12:43,892 --> 00:12:45,392
Step.

295
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,680
How did it get on?

296
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:49,100
I put it on to scare Chandler.

297
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,100
Oh, my God!

298
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:53,500
Monica's going to totally freak out!

299
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:55,720
Plus, it smells really bad in here.

300
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:57,460
Of course it smells bad.

301
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:59,800
You have your head up a turkey's ass.

302
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,240
Monica.

303
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:07,960
Did you get the turkey--?

304
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:10,000
Oh, my God!

305
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,260
Who is that?

306
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:13,740
It's Joey.

307
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:16,480
I got it!

308
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:17,880
If we win,

309
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:19,380
they have to get rid of the rooster.

310
00:13:19,975 --> 00:13:21,655
That's interesting!

311
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,100
If you win...

312
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,420
...we give up the bird.

313
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:30,780
But if we win...

314
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,840
...we get your apartment.

315
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:37,640
- Deal! - What?

316
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,500
"What was Monica's nickname

317
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,100
when she was a hockey goalie?"

318
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:43,300
- Big Fat Goalie. - Correct!

319
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:47,800
"Rachel claims it's her favorite movie."

320
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:48,640
<i>Dangerous Liaisons</i>.

321
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,940
Correct, "Her actual favorite movie is...?"

322
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:51,760
<i>Weekend at Bernie's</i>.

323
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:56,200
"Monica categorizes her towels.

324
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,300
How many categories are there?"

325
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,030
- Everyday use. - Fancy.

326
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:01,500
- Guest. - Fancy guest.

327
00:14:01,620 --> 00:14:02,460
- Two seconds. - Eleven?

328
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,020
Eleven! Unbelievable! Eleven is correct.

329
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:10,160
"Chandler was how old

330
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:11,740
when he first touched a girl's breast?"

331
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:13,240
- 14? - No, 19.

332
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:13,820
Thanks, man.

333
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:17,660
"Joey had an imaginary childhood friend.

334
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:19,040
- His name was...?" - Maurice!

335
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:20,380
Correct! "His profession was...?"

336
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:21,220
Space cowboy!

337
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:25,160
"What is Chandler Bing's job?"

338
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:31,620
Ten seconds.

339
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:32,460
You need this or you lose.

340
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:34,900
Something to do with transponding.

341
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:37,900
He's a transpons...transponster!

342
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,080
That's not even a word!

343
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:54,200
You are mean boys

344
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,640
who are just being mean!

345
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:56,820
Don't get mad!

346
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:59,140
No one forced you to raise the stakes.

347
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:01,480
That is not true! She forced me!

348
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,100
Hey, we would still be living here

349
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,440
if you hadn't gotten the question wrong!

350
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:06,660
It was a stupid, unfair question!

351
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:08,460
Don't blame the questions!

352
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:11,380
Stop yelling in our apartment!

353
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:13,520
You are ruining moving day for us.

354
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,560
Chandler!

355
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:21,780
I saw what you were doing in the window!

356
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,280
I saw what you're doing to my sister!

357
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,220
Get out here!

358
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:28,440
Listen, we had a good run.

359
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:31,040
What was it? Four, five months?

360
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,280
I mean that's more

361
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:33,440
than most people have in a lifetime.

362
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:34,700
So, goodbye, take care, byebye.

363
00:15:37,490 --> 00:15:37,940
Hey, Ross.

364
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:38,480
What's up, bro?

365
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:45,260
What the hell are you doing?

366
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:46,480
What's going on?

367
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:49,840
I think...I think Ross knows about me and Monica.

368
00:15:52,060 --> 00:15:53,640
Dude, he's right there.

369
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:57,840
I thought you were my best friend!

370
00:15:57,840 --> 00:15:59,220
This is my sister!

371
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,320
My best friend and my sister!

372
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:02,920
I cannot believe this!

373
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,720
We're not just messing around.

374
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,120
I love her.

375
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:08,340
I'm in love with her.

376
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:10,700
I'm so sorry

377
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:12,100
that you had to find out this way.

378
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:15,180
I'm sorry, but it's true.

379
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:16,480
I love him too.

380
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,080
My best friend and my sister!

381
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:30,960
I cannot believe this!

382
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:34,160
This is the last box of your clothes.

383
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:35,920
I'm just gonna label it

384
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:37,040
"What were you thinking?"

385
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:41,180
I was gonna go across the hall

386
00:16:41,180 --> 00:16:42,580
and write that on Chandler.

387
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:47,860
Guys, I don't mean to make things worse, but...

388
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:50,300
...l don't want to live with Rachel anymore.

389
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:51,380
-What? -What?

390
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,240
You're so mean to each other.

391
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:55,340
I don't wanna end up like that with Rachel.

392
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:56,560
I still like you.

393
00:16:58,060 --> 00:16:59,680
That's fine because I'm not moving.

394
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:02,660
Phoebe, you gotta take her.

395
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:05,440
You know, I know I said some bad stuff...

396
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:07,920
...but Rachel has qualities

397
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:09,080
that make her a good roommate.

398
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:11,000
She gets tons of catalogs and she folds

399
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:13,800
she folds down the pages of things she thinks I'd like.

400
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:15,440
What else?

401
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:18,480
When I take a shower...

402
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:21,280
...she leaves me notes on the mirror.

403
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,620
I do. I do do that.

404
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:25,400
That's nice.

405
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:27,820
I like having things to read in the bathroom.

406
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:32,420
When I fall asleep on the couch...

407
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:35,920
...she covers me with a blanket.

408
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:39,720
Well, you know, I don't want you to be cold.

409
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,520
And when I told her

410
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:45,880
that I was gonna move in with Chandler...

411
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:49,040
...she was really supportive.

412
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,820
You were so great.

413
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:57,160
You made it so easy.

414
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,220
And now you have to leave.

415
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:04,940
And I have to live with a boy!

416
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:22,880
- She really left. - I know.

417
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:29,240
- Thank you. - No problem, roomie.

418
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:40,080
- Can I ask you a question? - Sure.

419
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,380
What the hell is that dog doing here?

420
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:46,180
A little toast here. Ding, ding!

421
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:48,360
I know this isn't exactly

422
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:50,160
the kind of Thanksgiving you planned...

423
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:53,660
...but for me this has been really great.

424
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:55,800
You know, I think because

425
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,320
it didn't involve divorce...

426
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,140
...or projectile vomiting.

427
00:19:02,040 --> 00:19:02,700
Anyway, I think if

428
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,020
you had gone to Vail...

429
00:19:04,140 --> 00:19:05,980
...or if you had been with your family,

430
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:08,400
or if you didn't have...

431
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,980
...syphilis and stuff...

432
00:19:12,660 --> 00:19:13,820
...we wouldn't be all together.

433
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,700
So I guess what I'm trying to say is...

434
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:18,560
...that I'm very thankful

435
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:21,240
that all of your Thanksgivings sucked.

436
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,580
- That's so sweet! - Thank you.

437
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,860
Here's to a lousy Christmas!

438
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,480
And a crappy New Year!

439
00:19:32,665 --> 00:19:34,665
Hear, hear!

440
00:19:40,807 --> 00:19:41,847
You can't move.

441
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:43,060
You just-- You just can't.

442
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:43,820
Rachel's right.

443
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:45,680
This is where you guys belong.

444
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:47,560
Yeah.You don't wanna live in Westchester.

445
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:49,200
That's the worst of the Chesters.

446
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:51,420
You know,

447
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:53,220
sometimes when I'm alone in my apartment,

448
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:54,340
I look over here...

449
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:57,140
...and you guys are just having dinner...

450
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:59,760
...or watching TV or something...

451
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:03,160
...but it makes me feel better.

452
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:04,600
And now when I look over,

453
00:20:04,660 --> 00:20:05,640
who am I gonna see?

454
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,520
The Gottliebs? The Yangs?

455
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:11,280
They don't make me feel so good.

456
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:15,480
Yeah. So don't move, okay?

457
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,440
Just stay here...

458
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:18,940
...and maybe close your blinds at night.

459
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:19,620
Hey.

460
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:26,480
Hello?

461
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:32,360
It's Nancy. They responded to our offer.

462
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:33,340
And?

463
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:37,860
Okay. Thanks.

464
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:41,800
They passed.

465
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:46,340
They said they won't go a penny under the asking price.

466
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:48,660
- We can't afford that. - I know.

467
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:53,100
Well, there you go.

468
00:20:58,060 --> 00:20:59,580
I'm really sorry, you guys.

469
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:01,360
Yeah, I'm sorry too.

470
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:04,400
I'm even more sorry that phone call didn't come...

471
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:06,180
...before I told you about looking through the window.

472
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:09,540
Yeah. Well, we're gonna let you be alone.

473
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:10,920
You gonna be okay?

474
00:21:11,060 --> 00:21:11,980
Yeah, we'll be okay.

475
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:12,960
Love you guys.

476
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,740
You know, I'm really sorry

477
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:19,320
I wasn't more supportive before.

478
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:19,860
That's okay.

479
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:20,540
We understand.

480
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:22,380
Yeah, and about this Nancy....

481
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:24,220
If you're not sleeping with her, should l?

482
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:33,640
I know there'll be other houses, but I just--

483
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:36,840
- I love that one so much. - Yeah.

484
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,960
Well, it's a good thing we got it then.

485
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:43,920
- What? - We got the house.

486
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:45,820
Oh, my God.

487
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:47,760
I didn't wanna tell you in front of them.

488
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:49,440
Oh my god, we got it?! We got the house?!

489
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:50,440
We're getting a house!

490
00:21:55,820 --> 00:21:58,080
- We're getting a house. - And a baby.

491
00:21:58,440 --> 00:21:59,500
We're growing up.

492
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:02,460
We sure are.

493
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:05,280
- Who's gonna tell them? - Not it!

494
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:06,360
Not it! Damn it!

495
00:22:12,213 --> 00:22:13,523
Rachel, this is yours.

496
00:22:14,133 --> 00:22:16,003
Why? What are these for?

497
00:22:16,074 --> 00:22:17,004
You'll see.

498
00:22:17,064 --> 00:22:18,864
All right, everybody open them.

499
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:23,340
Wow, this is so beautiful!

500
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,420
These are the ones I was looking at in the store!

501
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:28,320
- I know. - Oh, I love this!

502
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,760
A meatball sub!

503
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,040
Thanks!

504
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:34,060
Seriously, guys, what's going on?

505
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:35,020
What are these for?

506
00:22:35,340 --> 00:22:37,240
Well, I didn't know how to tell you before...

507
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:40,440
- ...but we got the house. - Enjoy!

508
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:46,660
What did they say?

